You're on MSTest 3.8.2 with .NET 9 — great. Here's the recommended pattern:

```csharp
[TestClass]
public class MyTests : IAsyncDisposable
{
    private readonly TestContext _testContext;

    // Constructor injection for TestContext (MSTest v3+)
    public MyTests(TestContext testContext)
    {
        _testContext = testContext;
        // Synchronous initialization here
    }

    // Async initialization — runs before each test
    [TestInitialize]
    public async Task SetupAsync()
    {
        // Async per-test setup
        await SomeServiceAsync();
    }

    // Class-level async init (runs once)
    [ClassInitialize]
    public static async Task ClassSetup(TestContext context)
    {
        // One-time async setup for all tests in the class
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void MyTest()
    {
        _testContext.WriteLine("Running test");
        Assert.IsTrue(true);
    }

    // Async cleanup
    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        // Async per-instance teardown
        await Task.CompletedTask;
    }
}
```

**Key points for MSTest 3.x:**

| Concern | Mechanism |
|---------|-----------|
| Sync init (per-test) | Constructor with `TestContext` parameter |
| Async init (per-test) | `[TestInitialize] async Task` method |
| Async init (once) | `[ClassInitialize] static async Task` |
| Async cleanup | Implement `IAsyncDisposable` |
| Sync cleanup | Implement `IDisposable` or `[TestCleanup]` |

Constructor injection of `TestContext` replaced the older `public TestContext TestContext { get; set; }` property pattern and is the modern recommended approach.
